separate repository (vocab-engine) with its own MIT licence, or the pack
data described below.

## Pack data

The data under `pack/` and `data/` (words, sentences, patterns, passages,
pinyin lessons and character hints) is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

This reflects upstream share-alike terms. The per-source record is in
`pack/attribution.json`:

- Vocabulary comes from complete-hsk-vocabulary (MIT), the HSK word lists
  by drkameleon: https://github.com/drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary
- English glosses originate from CC-CEDICT (CC BY-SA 4.0), via
  complete-hsk-vocabulary: https://cc-cedict.org/wiki/
- Frequency data (word order within a level, frequency tiers) comes from
  wordfreq (data CC BY-SA 4.0; wordfreq code is Apache-2.0 and not shipped):
  https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq
- Character hints come from Make Me a Hanzi (c) Shaunak Kishore and
  contributors, licensed LGPL-3.0-or-later. This glyph data keeps its own
  licence; the texts are in `LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt` and
  `LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt`: https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi
- Two hand-written character hints restate English Wiktionary glyph origins
  (CC BY-SA 4.0).
- Example sentences and patterns are hand-authored for this pack and are
  released under CC BY-SA 4.0.

Build-time tools used to construct this pack are used only while building
and ship nothing into the built output. They do not affect the licence of
the shipped code or pack data. See the "Sources and licences" table in
README.md for the full list of sources used per data type.
